back and then try to seduce me?

260
00:13:51,831 --> 00:13:53,131
Arthur did that?

261
00:13:53,199 --> 00:13:55,433
Mm-hmm. He even gave me this.

262
00:13:57,604 --> 00:13:58,669
Very impressive.

263
00:13:58,738 --> 00:14:00,698
What did you have
to do to get that?

264
00:14:00,740 --> 00:14:01,906
Nothing.

265
00:14:01,975 --> 00:14:04,374
He put it around my
neck and kissed my cheek

266
00:14:04,443 --> 00:14:05,443
and that was that.

267
00:14:07,480 --> 00:14:09,858
I would think that Arthur would
expect a little more in return

268
00:14:09,882 --> 00:14:11,316
for his generosity.

269
00:14:11,384 --> 00:14:14,853
Well, he can expect anything
he wants... he won't get it.

270
00:14:17,423 --> 00:14:19,324
But you could, David.

271
00:14:19,392 --> 00:14:21,625
Anything you want.

272
00:14:21,694 --> 00:14:23,328
And you don't need jewelry.

273
00:14:25,298 --> 00:14:30,034
Sally, you are a very
attractive woman,

274
00:14:30,103 --> 00:14:32,069
but that's not the reason
I came here tonight.

275
00:14:32,138 --> 00:14:35,506
Well, maybe I can
give you another reason.

276
00:14:39,746 --> 00:14:40,823
Hello.

277
00:14:40,847 --> 00:14:42,947
I was looking for you.

278
00:14:43,016 --> 00:14:44,615
I thought you might be thirsty.

279
00:14:44,684 --> 00:14:46,962
Well, you found me. Again.

280
00:14:46,986 --> 00:14:50,020
First with Arthur
and now with, um...

281
00:14:50,089 --> 00:14:52,624
David. Whatever.

282
00:14:52,692 --> 00:14:55,392
Listen, if you two
want to talk, I'll...

283
00:14:55,461 --> 00:14:56,627
No, no, no, I'll go.

284
00:14:56,696 --> 00:14:58,529
That's what Sally wants.

285
00:14:58,598 --> 00:15:01,432
Isn't it, Sally?

286
00:15:01,501 --> 00:15:03,767
Enjoy.

287
00:15:03,836 --> 00:15:05,803
Good night, David.

288
00:15:05,872 --> 00:15:07,571
Have a pleasant evening, Sal.

289
00:15:20,586 --> 00:15:22,453
Take me home with you.

290
00:15:22,521 --> 00:15:25,389
I don't think Bart
would like that much.

291
00:15:25,458 --> 00:15:27,325
But you would.

292
00:15:27,393 --> 00:15:29,560
I promise, David.

293
00:15:32,064 --> 00:15:35,233
I'll get the car.

294
00:15:37,770 --> 00:15:39,570
Oh.

295
00:15:39,639 --> 00:15:41,672
I'll meet you out front.

296
00:15:43,910 --> 00:15:47,011
The guy gave me five bucks...

297
00:15:47,080 --> 00:15:49,157
Excuse me. The red Alpha please.

298
00:15:49,181 --> 00:15:50,848
Yes, sir.

299
00:15:50,917 --> 00:15:54,051
<i>"All right, no story.</i>

300
00:15:54,120 --> 00:15:56,320
<i>"But I wasn't going to
go home empty-handed.</i>

301
00:15:56,388 --> 00:15:59,423
<i>I felt pretty damn good."</i>

302
00:16:00,893 --> 00:16:02,638
Oh, my Lord,
somebody get a doctor...

303
00:16:02,662 --> 00:16:05,530
Mr. Tanney, will you come
back inside with us, please?

304
00:16:05,598 --> 00:16:07,838
Mr. Richardson's orders. What?

305
00:16:25,818 --> 00:16:26,818
You killed her.

306
00:16:30,556 --> 00:16:34,425
No, I didn't.

307
00:16:50,977 --> 00:16:54,045
<i>"I, Arthur Richardson, do
solemnly swear and affirm</i>

308
00:16:54,114 --> 00:16:57,047
<i>"that the following
statement is true and correct.</i>

309
00:16:57,116 --> 00:17:00,417
<i>"I loved parties,
especially my own.</i>

310
00:17:00,486 --> 00:17:03,154
<i>"But I was out of sorts
with Jan that night.</i>

311
00:17:03,222 --> 00:17:04,667
<i>"I couldn't wait to see her face</i>

312
00:17:04,691 --> 00:17:06,757
<i>when Sally Hitchcock arrived."</i>

313
00:17:06,826 --> 00:17:08,003
Keep smiling, darling.

314
00:17:08,027 --> 00:17:09,894
Just a couple of
hundred or so to go.

315
00:17:09,962 --> 00:17:11,662
I can take if you can, darling.

316
00:17:11,731 --> 00:17:14,132
Bart, you're alone.

317
00:17:14,200 --> 00:17:16,500
I'm meeting Sally here.

318
00:17:16,569 --> 00:17:18,503
Sally Hitchcock?

319
00:17:18,571 --> 00:17:21,706
I didn't know she was coming.

320
00:17:21,774 --> 00:17:23,552
You don't mind, do you, darling?

321
00:17:23,576 --> 00:17:26,043
Of course not, darling.

322
00:17:26,112 --> 00:17:27,389
I haven't seen her yet, Bart.

323
00:17:27,413 --> 00:17:29,013
Where's the bar?

324
00:17:29,082 --> 00:17:31,883
I've had the kind of day that
requires some serious unwinding.

325
00:17:40,292 --> 00:17:42,793
Sally darling.

326
00:17:42,862 --> 00:17:44,995
You know Jan.

327
00:17:45,064 --> 00:17:46,597
I feel as if I do.

328
00:17:46,666 --> 00:17:48,110
We have so much in common.

329
00:17:48,134 --> 00:17:50,634
Sally, behave yourself.

330
00:17:50,703 --> 00:17:52,370
Oh, Arthur, in the old days,

331
00:17:52,438 --> 00:17:54,583
you never would have
wanted me to behave myself.

332
00:17:54,607 --> 00:17:56,374
Quite the contrary.

333
00:17:56,442 --> 00:17:58,476
Sally, you look
great. Hello, Bart.

334
00:17:58,544 --> 00:18:00,010
You know Jan?

335
00:18:00,079 --> 00:18:01,879
Of course.

336
00:18:01,947 --> 00:18:04,081
Bart is my oldest
friend in Atlanta.

337
00:18:04,149 --> 00:18:06,049
In fact, he introduced
me to Arthur.

338
00:18:06,119 --> 00:18:08,118
How nice.

339
00:18:08,187 --> 00:18:11,489
Yes. We were living together
at the time, weren't we, Bart?

340
00:18:11,557 --> 00:18:13,090
But Arthur wanted me

341
00:18:13,159 --> 00:18:14,691
and Bart wanted
funding for Hess Towers

342
00:18:14,760 --> 00:18:16,527
so these two did what
businessmen do...

343
00:18:16,596 --> 00:18:18,028
They struck a deal.

344
00:18:18,098 --> 00:18:21,064
Well, that's an interesting
version of ancient history.

345
00:18:21,133 --> 00:18:22,845
Do you want to hear more, Jan?

346
00:18:22,869 --> 00:18:24,001
God no.

347
00:18:24,070 --> 00:18:25,647
You need a drink, darling.

348
00:18:25,671 --> 00:18:27,205
I won't argue with that.

349
00:18:27,273 --> 00:18:29,907
I need to speak to you
in private in a little while.

350
00:18:29,976 --> 00:18:30,908
All right.

351
00:18:30,977 --> 00:18:32,577
Promise? Promise.

352
00:18:37,983 --> 00:18:40,685
What was that about?

353
00:18:40,753 --> 00:18:42,119
I haven't the faintest idea.

354
00:18:42,188 --> 00:18:43,520
Come on, let's dance.

355
00:18:49,027 --> 00:18:52,107
<i>"I had a pretty good idea
what was on Sally's mind,</i>

356
00:18:52,164 --> 00:18:54,131
<i>and I was prepared for it."</i>

357
00:18:54,199 --> 00:18:56,333
What's this about, Sally?

358
00:18:56,402 --> 00:18:59,503
I'm still in love with
you, Arthur. Really?

359
00:18:59,572 --> 00:19:01,638
Well, I'm flattered, of course,

360
00:19:01,707 --> 00:19:03,841
but that's all in the past.

361
00:19:03,910 --> 00:19:05,476
I want you back.

362
00:19:05,545 --> 00:19:10,046
Well, you have heard,
I'm living with Jan.

363
00:19:10,116 --> 00:19:12,516
Jan's no problem.

364
00:19:12,585 --> 00:19:14,385
What do you mean?

365
00:19:14,453 --> 00:19:16,354
I mean I want you.

366
00:19:16,422 --> 00:19:18,489
I don't mind sharing you.

367
00:19:18,557 --> 00:19:19,623
Is that clear enough?

368
00:19:19,692 --> 00:19:22,192
Quite.

369
00:19:22,261 --> 00:19:23,973
But, of course, there's
another small problem.

370
00:19:23,997 --> 00:19:27,365
You affection is no
longer reciprocated.

371
00:19:32,438 --> 00:19:35,306
You can feel my
body this close to you

372
00:19:35,375 --> 00:19:37,415
and still say you
don't want me, Arthur?

373
00:19:37,476 --> 00:19:40,077
It's hard to believe, isn't it?

374
00:19:40,145 --> 00:19:41,645
Impossible.

375
00:19:49,488 --> 00:19:52,356
I love Jan very, very much

376
00:19:52,425 --> 00:19:54,525
and I've no desire
to cheat on her.

377
00:19:54,593 --> 00:19:56,092
At least, not yet.

378
00:19:57,864 --> 00:20:01,699
And not with someone
I've already had.

379
00:20:01,768 --> 00:20:05,202
You have a very charming way
of expressing yourself, Arthur.

380
00:20:05,270 --> 00:20:07,370
Now don't be offended, Sally.

381
00:20:07,440 --> 00:20:10,774
I've got a little
something for you.

382
00:20:10,843 --> 00:20:13,010
A souvenir of our relationship.

383
00:20:13,079 --> 00:20:14,144
A final souvenir.

384
00:20:16,349 --> 00:20:17,993
Oh, this is a payoff, Arthur?

385
00:20:18,017 --> 00:20:19,149
A trinket?

386
00:20:19,218 --> 00:20:23,387
Well, have a look before
you turn your nose up at it.

387
00:20:24,891 --> 00:20:27,891
Arthur!

388
00:20:27,960 --> 00:20:33,297
Here. A little something
to remember us by.

389
00:20:33,365 --> 00:20:34,698
Oh.

390
00:20:34,767 --> 00:20:36,366
Let's see what it
looks like on you.

391
00:20:43,208 --> 00:20:45,776
Oh, Arthur, it's beautiful.

392
00:20:45,845 --> 00:20:49,212
It's almost as beautiful
as you are, my dear.

393
00:20:54,987 --> 00:20:58,689
And now I think it's time
that we get back to the party.

394
00:21:03,896 --> 00:21:06,030
Mr. Matlock.

395
00:21:06,098 --> 00:21:08,765
Oh, hello, Gert.

396
00:21:08,835 --> 00:21:10,534
Oh, look at this.

397
00:21:10,602 --> 00:21:12,136
You're into mischief.

398
00:21:12,205 --> 00:21:14,638
Just working.

399
00:21:14,707 --> 00:21:16,551
You have been to the bathroom

400
00:21:16,575 --> 00:21:19,376
without calling for
me, haven't you?

401
00:21:19,445 --> 00:21:22,379
Well, I went just a little bit.

402
00:21:22,448 --> 00:21:23,914
How'd you know?

403
00:21:23,983 --> 00:21:25,582
I know the type.

404
00:21:27,619 --> 00:21:29,553
Gert, don't do that.

405
00:21:29,621 --> 00:21:31,788
I have those depositions
just the way I need them.

406
00:21:31,858 --> 00:21:33,190
Now it's going to take hours

407
00:21:33,259 --> 00:21:34,859
to get them back
the way they were.

408
00:21:34,927 --> 00:21:36,793
Don't you have any
sick people to tend to?

409
00:21:36,863 --> 00:21:40,431
I told the doctor about you,
and he said no work or else.

410
00:21:40,500 --> 00:21:41,565
Or else what?

411
00:21:41,634 --> 00:21:44,235
Or else a little of
this or a little of that.

412
00:21:44,303 --> 00:21:46,470
Maybe even a little shot.

413
00:21:46,538 --> 00:21:52,710
You tell that doctor to bring
anything he wants to in here.

414
00:21:52,778 --> 00:21:54,812
I'll take him to his knees

415
00:21:54,880 --> 00:21:57,014
and I'll hurt him every
way from Sunday

416
00:21:57,083 --> 00:21:58,827
and then we'll
see about no work.

417
00:21:58,851 --> 00:22:00,350
Mr. Matlock!

418
00:22:00,419 --> 00:22:03,286
Gert, I'm working
on a murder case.

419
00:22:03,355 --> 00:22:04,722
Murder one.

420
00:22:04,790 --> 00:22:07,424
The only thing standing
between my client

421
00:22:07,493 --> 00:22:08,759
and the maximum sentence

422
00:22:08,827 --> 00:22:10,461
is the best defense
I can prepare,

423
00:22:10,530 --> 00:22:12,530
and that's what I'm
doing, okay, Gert?

424
00:22:15,400 --> 00:22:21,371
Would you like pineapple
juice or nonfat egg-less custard?

425
00:22:25,077 --> 00:22:26,376
Custard.

426
00:22:30,849 --> 00:22:33,116
Hey, Gert.

427
00:22:33,185 --> 00:22:35,252
Two scoops.

428
00:22:35,321 --> 00:22:37,555
Hmm.

429
00:22:45,831 --> 00:22:48,432
Oh, really...?

430
00:22:48,500 --> 00:22:52,703
Now, ladies, not
arguing about me I hope.

431
00:22:52,772 --> 00:22:55,339
Oh, you would just love
that, wouldn't you, Arthur?

432
00:22:57,343 --> 00:22:59,976
What was that all about?

433
00:23:00,045 --> 00:23:02,712
Just Sally being a bitch.

434
00:23:13,393 --> 00:23:16,693
<i>Sally was being Sally</i>

435
00:23:16,763 --> 00:23:19,296
<i>and Bart, who should have
known better, was clearly furious.</i>

436
00:24:08,114 --> 00:24:10,814
My God, she's dead.

437
00:24:10,883 --> 00:24:12,883
Call the police.

438
00:24:12,952 --> 00:24:15,072
Where's Tanney? He
was just in here with her.

439
00:24:15,121 --> 00:24:16,220
Find him.

440
00:24:21,427 --> 00:24:22,726
Lights out.

441
00:24:22,795 --> 00:24:24,795
Oh, come on, Gert.

442
00:24:24,864 --> 00:24:26,074
You need your sleep.

443
00:24:26,098 --> 00:24:28,431
Gert, give me a break.

444
00:24:28,500 --> 00:24:30,701
Your doctor ordered
complete rest.

445
00:24:30,769 --> 00:24:32,636
He'll be very unhappy with you.

446
00:24:32,705 --> 00:24:34,838
Gert, you bring
that doctor in here,

447
00:24:34,907 --> 00:24:36,785
I'll throw his hind end
through that window

448
00:24:36,809 --> 00:24:38,876
and he'll be very
unhappy with you.

449
00:24:38,945 --> 00:24:40,777
Well, maybe tomorrow.

450
00:24:40,846 --> 00:24:43,013
But tonight, it's lights out.

451
00:24:43,082 --> 00:24:44,381
Oh, Gert.

452
00:24:44,450 --> 00:24:47,417
No. Good night, Mr. Matlock.

453
00:24:47,486 --> 00:24:49,486
Good night, Gert.

454
00:24:49,554 --> 00:24:51,488
<i>Gertrude.</i>

455
00:25:21,587 --> 00:25:23,787
Mr. Matlock.

456
00:25:23,856 --> 00:25:26,857
You're in deep trouble, Gert.

457
00:25:29,562 --> 00:25:32,696
<i>I, Barton Hess, do
solemnly swear and affirm</i>

458
00:25:32,765 --> 00:25:35,766
<i>that the following
statement is true and correct.</i>

459
00:25:35,835 --> 00:25:37,167
Evening, sir.

460
00:25:39,871 --> 00:25:41,671
<i>I couldn't wait to see Sally.</i>

461
00:25:41,740 --> 00:25:43,073
<i>We were getting along so well,</i>

462
00:25:43,142 --> 00:25:45,775
<i>like old times, only better.</i>

463
00:25:49,715 --> 00:25:51,614
Bart. Oh.

464
00:25:51,684 --> 00:25:53,449
You're alone?

465
00:25:53,519 --> 00:25:54,684
Uh, I'm meeting Sally here.

466
00:25:54,754 --> 00:25:57,120
Sally Hitchcock?

467
00:25:57,189 --> 00:25:59,623
I didn't know she was coming.

468
00:25:59,692 --> 00:26:01,325
Well, yes.

469
00:26:01,393 --> 00:26:03,438
You don't mind, do you, darling?

470
00:26:03,462 --> 00:26:05,462
Of course not, darling.

471
00:26:09,034 --> 00:26:10,545
She hasn't arrived yet, Bart.

472
00:26:10,569 --> 00:26:13,804
Tell her I'm here,
will you, Arthur?

473
00:26:13,872 --> 00:26:15,338
It's nice to see you, Jan.

474
00:26:17,943 --> 00:26:19,520
Arthur. Sally.

475
00:26:19,544 --> 00:26:21,624
How are you? Good.

476
00:26:24,350 --> 00:26:26,783
Oh, Bart, sweetheart.

477
00:26:27,786 --> 00:26:30,420
You look... delicious.

478
00:26:31,657 --> 00:26:32,756
Oh, do you know Jan?

479
00:26:32,825 --> 00:26:33,890
Of course.

480
00:26:33,960 --> 00:26:35,770
Bart is my oldest
friend in Atlanta.

481
00:26:35,794 --> 00:26:38,062
In fact, he introduced
me to Arthur.

482
00:26:38,130 --> 00:26:40,175
Um, it's ancient history.

483
00:26:40,199 --> 00:26:41,709
You want to hear more, Jan?

484
00:26:41,733 --> 00:26:43,733
Not really.

485
00:26:43,802 --> 00:26:45,702
Except that he's also
my dearest friend.

486
00:26:45,771 --> 00:26:48,050
Well, thank you, sweetheart.
That deserves champagne.

487
00:26:48,074 --> 00:26:49,906
Oh, I'd love some.

488
00:26:51,977 --> 00:26:53,722
<i>In the old days, I
would have been uneasy</i>

489
00:26:53,746 --> 00:26:57,580
<i>seeing them together, but
I pushed aside any doubts.</i>

490
00:26:59,118 --> 00:27:00,550
What was that all about?

491
00:27:00,619 --> 00:27:02,252
What? Arthur.

492
00:27:02,321 --> 00:27:03,464
Oh. What did he want?

493
00:27:03,488 --> 00:27:04,799
He said he wanted
to talk to me later.

494
00:27:04,823 --> 00:27:06,156
Oh? About what?

495
00:27:06,225 --> 00:27:07,791
I don't know.

496
00:27:07,860 --> 00:27:10,105
It is over between
you and him, isn't it?

497
00:27:10,129 --> 00:27:11,628
Of course it is, darling.

498
00:27:11,696 --> 00:27:13,230
Don't be silly.

499
00:27:13,298 --> 00:27:15,632
I am right where
I belong: with you.

500
00:27:29,115 --> 00:27:31,675
Excuse me, Miss Hitchcock.

501
00:27:33,952 --> 00:27:35,252
I won't be long, darling.

502
00:27:41,927 --> 00:27:43,638
<i>I knew she was
going to see Arthur.</i>

503
00:27:43,662 --> 00:27:44,873
<i>Some men would have been angry,</i>

504
00:27:44,897 --> 00:27:47,831
<i>but I prided myself
on my equanimity.</i>

505
00:27:47,900 --> 00:27:50,133
<i>Besides, I trusted
Sally completely.</i>

506
00:27:54,873 --> 00:27:56,807
Sally!

507
00:28:07,253 --> 00:28:10,120
<i>I noticed there was
something different immediately.</i>

508
00:28:10,188 --> 00:28:11,555
<i>A necklace.</i>

509
00:28:11,624 --> 00:28:13,234
<i>I decided not to
ask Sally about it,</i>

510
00:28:13,258 --> 00:28:14,625
<i>but to let her tell me.</i>

511
00:28:14,693 --> 00:28:16,326
Hi.

512
00:28:16,394 --> 00:28:18,294
I need some champagne.

513
00:28:18,363 --> 00:28:19,629
What did he want?

514
00:28:19,698 --> 00:28:20,842
You won't believe this.

515
00:28:20,866 --> 00:28:23,533
About Arthur? I'd
believe anything.

516
00:28:23,602 --> 00:28:25,035
He made a pass at me.

517
00:28:25,103 --> 00:28:27,070
Isn't that bizarre?

518
00:28:27,139 --> 00:28:28,272
What do you mean?

519
00:28:28,340 --> 00:28:29,951
I mean, he tried to
seduce me, darling.

520
00:28:29,975 --> 00:28:31,074
The gold treatment.

521
00:28:31,143 --> 00:28:32,276
He said he missed me.

522
00:28:32,344 --> 00:28:33,977
He said he thought
about me constantly,

523
00:28:34,046 --> 00:28:35,512
wished we were still together.

524
00:28:35,581 --> 00:28:37,481
Oh, then he kissed me.

525
00:28:37,550 --> 00:28:40,117
And, how do I put this?

526
00:28:40,185 --> 00:28:42,185
He, um... He wouldn't let me go.

527
00:28:42,254 --> 00:28:43,487
What did you say?

528
00:28:43,556 --> 00:28:45,688
I said I loved you,

529
00:28:45,757 --> 00:28:48,392
and that our
relationship was serious

530
00:28:48,460 --> 00:28:50,793
and I'd never do
anything to jeopardize it.

531
00:28:50,862 --> 00:28:52,796
How did he take that?

532
00:28:52,865 --> 00:28:54,832
Pretty well, actually.

533
00:28:54,900 --> 00:28:56,399
But then, what could he do?

534
00:28:56,469 --> 00:28:58,702
I mean, he knew I
meant exactly what I said.

535
00:28:58,771 --> 00:29:01,438
And just to prove there were
no hard feelings, he gave me this.

536
00:29:01,507 --> 00:29:05,375
That's a parting gift, I hope.

537
00:29:05,444 --> 00:29:07,177
For old times' sake.

538
00:29:07,246 --> 00:29:08,979
Well, Arthur's got style.

539
00:29:09,048 --> 00:29:10,314
I'll give him that.

540
00:29:10,382 --> 00:29:12,215
Sally.

541
00:29:12,284 --> 00:29:13,483
Hello, David.

542
00:29:13,552 --> 00:29:15,764
Excuse me. Sally, you
look absolutely gorgeous.

543
00:29:15,788 --> 00:29:17,888
Thank you. You
remember Bart, don't you?

544
00:29:17,957 --> 00:29:20,023
Oh, yes, hi. How are you?

545
00:29:20,092 --> 00:29:21,425
Fine. How about you?

546
00:29:21,493 --> 00:29:22,926
Just fine.

547
00:29:22,994 --> 00:29:24,154
Sally, we must talk.

548
00:29:24,196 --> 00:29:26,774
Um... That's my
cue for champagne.

549
00:29:26,798 --> 00:29:28,865
Thank you,
sweetheart. Hurry back.

550
00:29:33,171 --> 00:29:34,916
<i>I wondered what
they were talking about</i>

551
00:29:34,940 --> 00:29:36,206
<i>and then I reminded myself,</i>

552
00:29:36,275 --> 00:29:38,775
<i>"I trust Sally completely."</i>

553
00:29:41,814 --> 00:29:43,725
Here you are, darling.
Oh, thank you, sweetheart.

554
00:29:43,749 --> 00:29:47,084
David was just telling me
about investigative reporting.

555
00:29:47,153 --> 00:29:49,331
Oh, the fine art of the exposé.

556
00:29:49,355 --> 00:29:51,199
Whose trail are you hot on now?

557
00:29:51,223 --> 00:29:52,467
No one.

558
00:29:52,491 --> 00:29:55,051
But I am open to suggestions.

559
00:29:57,028 --> 00:29:58,973
Well, it's time
for me to mingle.

560
00:29:58,997 --> 00:30:00,363
I'll see you later.

561
00:30:03,902 --> 00:30:05,936
Abrupt, isn't he?

562
00:30:06,005 --> 00:30:07,215
Oh, yeah, somewhat of a hustler.

563
00:30:07,239 --> 00:30:08,672
Oh? Was he hustling you?

564
00:30:08,740 --> 00:30:10,051
No, not really. He
was just asking me

565
00:30:10,075 --> 00:30:11,541
reporter type questions.

566
00:30:11,610 --> 00:30:14,143
I suspect he thinks
I have secrets to tell.

567
00:30:14,213 --> 00:30:16,346
You're joking.

568
00:30:16,415 --> 00:30:18,949
Yes.

569
00:30:20,653 --> 00:30:22,485
Shall we dance? Mmm.

570
00:30:34,967 --> 00:30:36,510
Not arguing about me, I hope.

571
00:30:36,534 --> 00:30:39,435
You'd just love that,
wouldn't you, Arthur?

572
00:30:46,211 --> 00:30:48,044
Sally.

573
00:30:48,113 --> 00:30:49,212
What's the matter?

574
00:30:49,281 --> 00:30:50,480
Nothing.

575
00:30:50,548 --> 00:30:53,083
I think it's something.

576
00:30:53,151 --> 00:30:55,263
Jan's jealous and
taking it out on me.

577
00:30:55,287 --> 00:30:57,854
And why is she jealous?

578
00:30:57,922 --> 00:30:59,489
Jealousy is a way of life

579
00:30:59,557 --> 00:31:01,477
when you live with a
man as unfaithful as Arthur.

580
00:31:01,526 --> 00:31:04,086
Ah. Whatever you say, darling.

581
00:31:13,739 --> 00:31:15,239
What's this?

582
00:31:15,307 --> 00:31:18,208
Another little gift from Arthur.

583
00:31:18,277 --> 00:31:20,410
He scratched me when he
was putting on the necklace

584
00:31:20,479 --> 00:31:22,079
and then he insisted
on a bandage.

585
00:31:22,147 --> 00:31:24,348
Well, you know how
phobic he is about germs.

586
00:31:24,416 --> 00:31:26,976
Yes, Arthur does have
his, uh, idiosyncrasies.

587
00:31:27,019 --> 00:31:28,551
Tell me about it.

588
00:31:33,125 --> 00:31:35,525
Hi! I thought you
might be thirsty.

589
00:31:35,594 --> 00:31:37,672
I brought along some
of my private stock.

590
00:31:37,696 --> 00:31:39,707
Oh, thank you,
sweetheart. That's so sweet.

591
00:31:39,731 --> 00:31:41,197
Oh, where's you're glass, David?

592
00:31:41,267 --> 00:31:44,034
Actually, Sally and
I were just talking.

593
00:31:44,102 --> 00:31:46,536
Oh, I'm sorry. I didn't
mean to interrupt.

594
00:31:46,605 --> 00:31:47,749
You didn't.

595
00:31:47,773 --> 00:31:49,673
David is just being rude.

596
00:31:49,742 --> 00:31:51,074
No, no. I understand completely.

597
00:31:51,143 --> 00:31:53,510
Um... Enjoy the champagne.

598
00:31:53,579 --> 00:31:55,012
And the evening.

599
00:31:55,080 --> 00:31:56,413
See you later, Sally.

600
00:32:24,309 --> 00:32:26,743
What happened?

601
00:32:32,084 --> 00:32:33,516
She's dead.

602
00:32:34,620 --> 00:32:36,385
Call the police.

603
00:32:36,454 --> 00:32:38,055
David Tanney.

604
00:32:38,123 --> 00:32:39,200
He was just in here with her.

605
00:32:39,224 --> 00:32:41,191
Get him.

606
00:32:53,772 --> 00:32:56,472
You killed her.

607
00:33:08,220 --> 00:33:09,364
Good morning.

608
00:33:09,388 --> 00:33:10,586
Oh, hi, Gert.

609
00:33:10,655 --> 00:33:11,988
Gertrude.

610
00:33:12,057 --> 00:33:13,337
How did you sleep?

611
00:33:13,392 --> 00:33:15,325
Fine, fine, fine, fine, fine.

612
00:33:15,394 --> 00:33:17,171
Well, you sound a
little more chipper today.

613
00:33:17,195 --> 00:33:18,794
Oh, yeah, I feel good.

614
00:33:18,863 --> 00:33:20,596
A little headache, but...

615
00:33:20,665 --> 00:33:23,225
Oh, well, we can
take care of that.

616
00:33:23,402 --> 00:33:24,734
Yeah?

617
00:33:24,802 --> 00:33:26,903
What's that, a mustard plaster?

618
00:33:26,971 --> 00:33:28,571
It's a patch.

619
00:33:28,640 --> 00:33:30,407
Don't you have
any headache pills?

620
00:33:30,476 --> 00:33:31,942
This is better than a pill.

621
00:33:32,010 --> 00:33:33,154
It doesn't upset your stomach

622
00:33:33,178 --> 00:33:35,056
and it keeps
working much longer.

623
00:33:35,080 --> 00:33:38,014
The medication is in the bandage

624
00:33:38,083 --> 00:33:41,918
and it leeches into the skin
a little at a time by osmosis.

625
00:33:41,987 --> 00:33:45,955
You know what
osmosis is, don't you

626
00:33:46,024 --> 00:33:48,758
I did in high school.

627
00:33:48,827 --> 00:33:50,760
Give me your arm.

628
00:33:55,099 --> 00:33:57,033
Osmosis.

629
00:34:00,472 --> 00:34:04,974
Gert... I love you.

630
00:34:20,426 --> 00:34:22,358
Now, do this, Michelle.

631
00:34:22,428 --> 00:34:25,261
Catch her the minute
she gets to the courthouse.

632
00:34:25,330 --> 00:34:27,030
Get her off by herself.

633
00:34:27,098 --> 00:34:30,567
Because she won't talk to you
if Arthur Richardson is around.

634
00:34:30,636 --> 00:34:32,335
Okay? Okay.

635
00:34:34,840 --> 00:34:36,272
Oh, hi, Charlie.

636
00:34:36,341 --> 00:34:38,642
I thought maybe
you'd get in early today.

637
00:34:38,710 --> 00:34:39,921
Morning, Ben, what
happened to you?

638
00:34:39,945 --> 00:34:41,077
I got hit by a car.

639
00:34:41,146 --> 00:34:42,390
Damn crazy drivers.

640
00:34:42,414 --> 00:34:43,591
You know, a cousin of
mine just got hit by a car.

641
00:34:43,615 --> 00:34:44,981
No, no, it was my fault.

642
00:34:45,050 --> 00:34:47,261
I got absentminded and I wasn't
watching where I was going.

643
00:34:47,285 --> 00:34:48,630
You got to be careful, Ben.

644
00:34:48,654 --> 00:34:50,031
I wouldn't like to see
you in here as a customer,

645
00:34:50,055 --> 00:34:51,265
if you know what I mean.

646
00:34:51,289 --> 00:34:52,767
Yeah.

647
00:34:52,791 --> 00:34:58,494
Yeah... Boy, you're
running out of space.

648
00:34:58,563 --> 00:35:00,603
Dead people leave
a lot of stuff behind.

649
00:35:00,665 --> 00:35:03,133
You know, the corpus delicti
go in an ice box down the hall.

650
00:35:03,201 --> 00:35:04,812
Everything else
winds up in here.

651
00:35:04,836 --> 00:35:07,136
Well, that's why I
stopped by, Charlie.

652
00:35:07,205 --> 00:35:10,673
Um... You want to turn around?

653
00:35:15,046 --> 00:35:18,381
I, uh... I'm stuck on a case,

654
00:35:18,450 --> 00:35:22,519
and I think there may be a
piece of evidence I missed.

655
00:35:22,588 --> 00:35:24,499
Well, the DA's office
keeps the real evidence.

656
00:35:24,523 --> 00:35:27,490
All I got is odds and
ends and leftover junk.

657
00:35:27,559 --> 00:35:29,892
Well, that may be just
exactly what I'm looking for.

658
00:35:29,961 --> 00:35:32,696
Here-Here's the
case... the case number.

659
00:35:32,764 --> 00:35:34,164
Can I turn around?

660
00:35:34,232 --> 00:35:35,232
Turn around.

661
00:35:48,146 --> 00:35:50,179
Oh, excuse me.

662
00:35:50,248 --> 00:35:52,949
Ben, how are you feeling?

663
00:35:53,018 --> 00:35:54,550
Oh, I feel fine.

664
00:35:54,619 --> 00:35:55,785
You look awful.

665
00:35:55,854 --> 00:35:56,894
I do?

666
00:35:56,955 --> 00:36:00,123
Yes. Terrible.

667
00:36:00,192 --> 00:36:02,425
Did you talk to Jan?

668
00:36:02,494 --> 00:36:04,160
Yeah, you were right.

669
00:36:04,229 --> 00:36:05,539
Yeah? Yeah.

670
00:36:05,563 --> 00:36:07,608
Do you know what I
was trying to think of

671
00:36:07,632 --> 00:36:08,564
when that car hit me?

672
00:36:08,633 --> 00:36:09,765
Yeah. Did you figure it out?

673
00:36:09,834 --> 00:36:11,301
Yep.

674
00:36:11,370 --> 00:36:15,004
In the hospital, I
had such a headache

675
00:36:15,073 --> 00:36:17,618
from the... from the
accident and from reading

676
00:36:17,642 --> 00:36:21,544
all those depositions, and
this nurse cured it for me.

677
00:36:21,612 --> 00:36:23,112
Wonderful woman. Oh...

678
00:36:23,181 --> 00:36:24,692
Yeah, and that's
what did it, yeah.

679
00:36:24,716 --> 00:36:25,960
Did what? Yeah.

680
00:36:25,984 --> 00:36:27,617
Did what?

681
00:36:32,791 --> 00:36:34,891
Court will come to order.

682
00:36:34,959 --> 00:36:38,161
Court is pleased to see
Mr. Matlock back with us so soon.

683
00:36:38,230 --> 00:36:39,462
Glad to be back, Your Honor.

684
00:36:39,531 --> 00:36:40,897
I apologize for my appearance.

685
00:36:40,965 --> 00:36:42,177
If you're ready to proceed,

686
00:36:42,201 --> 00:36:43,944
you may call your first witness.

687
00:36:43,968 --> 00:36:45,235
Thank you.

688
00:36:45,304 --> 00:36:48,871
Uh, I call Arthur
Richardson to the stand,

689
00:36:48,940 --> 00:36:52,242
and, uh, since he's already
testified for the prosecution,

690
00:36:52,311 --> 00:36:55,312
I request permission
to examine him

691
00:36:55,380 --> 00:36:57,425
as a hostile witness
during his testimony.

692
00:36:57,449 --> 00:37:00,149
Permission granted.
Proceed, Mr. Matlock.

693
00:37:00,219 --> 00:37:04,787
Mr. Richardson, for several
months before she was killed,

694
00:37:04,856 --> 00:37:08,458
you were having an
affair with Sally Hitchcock,

695
00:37:08,527 --> 00:37:09,527
isn't that right?

696
00:37:09,594 --> 00:37:10,760
It was no secret, yes.

697
00:37:10,828 --> 00:37:15,131
Yep. And even after
the affair was over,

698
00:37:15,199 --> 00:37:17,634
you, um, as they
say, uh, kept in touch?

699
00:37:17,702 --> 00:37:18,835
Oh, yes.

700
00:37:18,903 --> 00:37:20,681
I even invited
her to my parties.

701
00:37:20,705 --> 00:37:22,382
Why did you invite
to your parties?

702
00:37:22,406 --> 00:37:23,518
She was beautiful, charming,

703
00:37:23,542 --> 00:37:25,574
and I was very fond of her.

704
00:37:25,643 --> 00:37:28,478
Mm, mm.

705
00:37:28,547 --> 00:37:31,915
Did you know that, uh...
she was planning to write

706
00:37:31,983 --> 00:37:36,352
one of those magazine
articles on you?

707
00:37:36,421 --> 00:37:39,389
Sally? Write?

708
00:37:39,457 --> 00:37:40,835
Obviously, you
didn't know Sally.

709
00:37:40,859 --> 00:37:42,292
No, no, I didn't, but, uh...

710
00:37:42,360 --> 00:37:44,494
lesser lights than
Miss Hitchcock

711
00:37:44,563 --> 00:37:45,962
have been published.

712
00:37:46,030 --> 00:37:48,075
All she needed was a
ghostwriter and something to say,

713
00:37:48,099 --> 00:37:50,678
and she had...
Objection: relevance.

714
00:37:50,702 --> 00:37:52,146
Sustained. Sally
had nothing to say.

715
00:37:52,170 --> 00:37:53,436
She had plenty to say.

716
00:37:53,505 --> 00:37:55,082
She was with you all the time.

717
00:37:55,106 --> 00:37:56,884
She knew all about
you, didn't she?

718
00:37:56,908 --> 00:37:58,908
I resent the insinuation.

719
00:37:58,977 --> 00:38:01,055
There's no insinuation.

720
00:38:01,079 --> 00:38:03,079
There's no insinuation.

721
00:38:03,148 --> 00:38:07,050
You keep a very high profile.

722
00:38:07,119 --> 00:38:08,684
A lot of good-looking women,

723
00:38:08,754 --> 00:38:12,856
a lot of money, lot
of powerful people.

724
00:38:12,924 --> 00:38:17,526
And, uh... she knew
all about your, uh...

725
00:38:19,865 --> 00:38:23,266
exploits... and,
well, idiosyncrasies.

726
00:38:23,334 --> 00:38:24,334
Didn't she?

727
00:38:24,402 --> 00:38:27,369
Mr. Matlock, I may be rich

728
00:38:27,438 --> 00:38:29,116
and I may throw
extravagant parties.

729
00:38:29,140 --> 00:38:31,273
But I'm a very ordinary person

730
00:38:31,342 --> 00:38:34,476
with a very uninteresting
personal life.

731
00:38:34,545 --> 00:38:38,881
Anybody who suggests
otherwise may find them self

732
00:38:38,950 --> 00:38:42,118
constrained to prove
those allegations in court.

733
00:38:42,187 --> 00:38:44,620
Yeah, yeah, yeah,
and that's what,

734
00:38:44,689 --> 00:38:47,457
that's what David
Tanney told her, wasn't it?

735
00:38:47,526 --> 00:38:53,496
He told her that she had to
have all her stories on you

736
00:38:53,565 --> 00:38:55,398
independently corroborated

737
00:38:55,466 --> 00:38:57,400
or no publisher
would touch them,

738
00:38:57,468 --> 00:38:59,869
and that's what she was
talking with Jan about...

739
00:38:59,938 --> 00:39:01,237
Corroboration, wasn't it?

740
00:39:01,305 --> 00:39:04,107
Well, you'll have to
ask Jan about that.

741
00:39:04,175 --> 00:39:05,442
Didn't Jan tell you

742
00:39:05,510 --> 00:39:07,622
that she was trying to
get corroboration on her?

743
00:39:07,646 --> 00:39:09,645
Jan said no such thing.

744
00:39:09,714 --> 00:39:10,913
She didn't?

745
00:39:10,982 --> 00:39:13,282
Huh. She didn't?

746
00:39:13,351 --> 00:39:18,320
My associate subpoenaed
her just this morning

747
00:39:18,390 --> 00:39:21,156
after you had come
in the courthouse

748
00:39:21,225 --> 00:39:23,671
before you had a
chance to speak with her.

749
00:39:23,695 --> 00:39:27,162
Are you sure she
wouldn't say...?

750
00:39:27,231 --> 00:39:28,409
Well, she might have mentioned

751
00:39:28,433 --> 00:39:29,510
something along
those lines, I...

752
00:39:29,534 --> 00:39:30,900
Along what lines?

753
00:39:30,969 --> 00:39:33,369
Something about some of
the things that happened.

754
00:39:33,438 --> 00:39:35,416
I don't know; I didn't
pay that much attention.

755
00:39:35,440 --> 00:39:39,842
No, no, no, you didn't.

756
00:39:39,911 --> 00:39:46,749
You didn't have to...
because you knew.

757
00:39:46,818 --> 00:39:50,586
Sally Hitchcock was
blackmailing you, wasn't she?

758
00:39:50,655 --> 00:39:53,956
I don't know what
you're talking about.

759
00:39:54,025 --> 00:39:55,636
And that's why she
was at the party.

760
00:39:55,660 --> 00:39:58,528
She was there because
she had a pretty face.

761
00:39:58,596 --> 00:40:00,007
That's what the
meeting was about

762
00:40:00,031 --> 00:40:02,264
up in your bedroom,
wasn't it: blackmail.

763
00:40:02,333 --> 00:40:03,800
No.

764
00:40:03,869 --> 00:40:08,605
And the big payoff was that
expensive necklace, wasn't it?

765
00:40:08,673 --> 00:40:10,518
Objection: relevancy;
badgering the witness.

766
00:40:10,542 --> 00:40:12,441
Sustained. Your Honor,

767
00:40:12,511 --> 00:40:19,148
I have gone through
every piece of testimony

768
00:40:19,216 --> 00:40:22,351
by every witness in this trial,

769
00:40:22,420 --> 00:40:25,354
and they're all
partly the truth.

770
00:40:25,423 --> 00:40:27,290
Some are complete,
some are incomplete.

771
00:40:27,359 --> 00:40:28,958
Some are partial,
some are impartial.

772
00:40:29,027 --> 00:40:32,728
But they're all inconsistent
with one another.

773
00:40:32,797 --> 00:40:37,300
We will find out what
happened that night,

774
00:40:37,369 --> 00:40:42,805
but I must beg the
court's indulgence, please.

775
00:40:42,874 --> 00:40:45,375
Proceed.

776
00:40:45,443 --> 00:40:47,076
Thank you.

777
00:40:47,144 --> 00:40:51,547
Now... that meeting...

778
00:40:51,616 --> 00:40:54,950
Talk... that you had with Sally

779
00:40:55,019 --> 00:40:56,853
up in, up in your bedroom,

780
00:40:56,921 --> 00:40:59,989
you were the only witness
to that conversation, right?

781
00:41:00,057 --> 00:41:01,391
Sadly.

782
00:41:01,459 --> 00:41:03,204
Why did you give
her that necklace?

783
00:41:03,228 --> 00:41:07,363
Just a little memento
for old time's sake.

784
00:41:07,431 --> 00:41:09,798
Oh, boy, that's gallant.

785
00:41:09,867 --> 00:41:14,169
I'm talking about
gallant, gallant.

786
00:41:14,239 --> 00:41:16,505
And did you put it
around her neck?

787
00:41:16,574 --> 00:41:18,140
Yes, as a matter of fact.

788
00:41:18,210 --> 00:41:19,776
And when you put it on her,

789
00:41:19,844 --> 00:41:22,178
you scratched her neck
a little bit, didn't you?

790
00:41:22,246 --> 00:41:23,146
No.

791
00:41:23,214 --> 00:41:26,181
Well, people at the party

792
00:41:26,250 --> 00:41:30,419
saw her when she came down
from the bedroom, said that...

793
00:41:30,488 --> 00:41:32,600
that she had a little patch
on the back of her neck.

794
00:41:32,624 --> 00:41:33,890
I don't remember that.

795
00:41:33,958 --> 00:41:36,259
Well, it's right here...

796
00:41:36,328 --> 00:41:39,195
in, uh, in the People's
autopsy report.

797
00:41:39,264 --> 00:41:40,063
See right here?

798
00:41:40,131 --> 00:41:41,430
Look right there.

799
00:41:41,499 --> 00:41:45,568
"A small laceration on the
back of the decedent's neck."

800
00:41:45,636 --> 00:41:48,103
I just don't recall that.

801
00:41:48,172 --> 00:41:49,238
Yeah.

802
00:41:49,307 --> 00:41:56,212
Well, uh, do you, do
you remember, uh...

803
00:41:56,281 --> 00:41:59,381
do you remember being
in-in-in the bathroom with her

804
00:41:59,450 --> 00:42:04,987
while she was admiring
the necklace in the mirror?

805
00:42:05,056 --> 00:42:08,023
You told the police that

806
00:42:08,092 --> 00:42:09,704
you were and it was
in your deposition.

807
00:42:09,728 --> 00:42:15,131
Well, she wanted to look
at the necklace in the mirror.

808
00:42:16,467 --> 00:42:18,545
Of course, you had a
big mirror in the bedroom

809
00:42:18,569 --> 00:42:20,703
and plenty of light.

810
00:42:20,772 --> 00:42:25,642
You took her in the
bathroom because you wanted

811
00:42:25,710 --> 00:42:29,245
to put a bandage on
that scratch, didn't you?

812
00:42:29,313 --> 00:42:32,215
Oh, yes, yes.

813
00:42:32,283 --> 00:42:34,228
Uh, I didn't recall
that at the time.

814
00:42:34,252 --> 00:42:35,396
You're right, I did, indeed.

815
00:42:35,420 --> 00:42:36,785
Your Honor, I have

816
00:42:36,854 --> 00:42:40,255
a continuing relevancy
objection to all of these questions.

817
00:42:40,324 --> 00:42:42,225
Your Honor, please?

818
00:42:42,293 --> 00:42:44,460
You need to move
on, Mr. Matlock.

819
00:42:44,529 --> 00:42:47,329
We are, Your Honor, we are.

820
00:42:47,398 --> 00:42:51,634
Uh, traces of poison were found

821
00:42:51,703 --> 00:42:54,804
in the decedent's
champagne glass.

822
00:42:54,873 --> 00:42:59,642
And the police assumed
that's what killed her.

823
00:42:59,711 --> 00:43:05,280
But that poison could
have been put in that glass

824
00:43:05,349 --> 00:43:11,888
by people who entered the
room after she had collapsed,

825
00:43:11,956 --> 00:43:15,057
and you were one
of them, weren't you?

826
00:43:15,126 --> 00:43:16,458
Yes.

827
00:43:16,528 --> 00:43:18,305
But why would I do
something like that?

828
00:43:18,329 --> 00:43:19,395
To cover your tracks.

829
00:43:19,464 --> 00:43:22,365
To throw off the police.

830
00:43:22,433 --> 00:43:26,802
Because, in fact...
you had poisoned her

831
00:43:26,871 --> 00:43:29,138
several hours
before, hadn't you?

832
00:43:29,207 --> 00:43:30,273
That's impossible!

833
00:43:30,342 --> 00:43:31,385
I know.

834
00:43:31,409 --> 00:43:33,042
I thought so, too.

835
00:43:33,111 --> 00:43:34,177
I thought so, too.

836
00:43:34,245 --> 00:43:35,945
I couldn't figure it out.

837
00:43:36,014 --> 00:43:37,913
I just couldn't figure it out.

838
00:43:37,983 --> 00:43:40,183
I brooded over it.

839
00:43:40,251 --> 00:43:42,685
I, finally, I was hit by a car.

840
00:43:42,753 --> 00:43:44,765
I had to go to the hospital.

841
00:43:44,789 --> 00:43:45,989
See?

842
00:43:46,057 --> 00:43:47,923
I had this awful headache.

843
00:43:47,993 --> 00:43:51,227
And this nurse,

844
00:43:51,296 --> 00:43:56,165
this wonderful, beautiful
nurse... Gertrude...

845
00:43:56,234 --> 00:43:59,135
She cured it for me.

846
00:43:59,204 --> 00:44:03,973
She, she, she gave me what
she called a "medication patch."

847
00:44:04,042 --> 00:44:06,220
I'd never seen
anything like that before.

848
00:44:06,244 --> 00:44:10,846
It's like a bandage that's
impregnated with medication.

849
00:44:10,915 --> 00:44:14,550
And you put it on, and it
goes through your system

850
00:44:14,619 --> 00:44:18,221
slowly over a
long period of time.

851
00:44:18,289 --> 00:44:23,559
And, finally, it finds the
pain and takes it away.

852
00:44:23,628 --> 00:44:24,908
Your Honor,

853
00:44:24,962 --> 00:44:29,132
now Mr. Matlock
is testifying for us.

854
00:44:29,200 --> 00:44:30,844
But, Your Honor,
my headache's gone.

855
00:44:30,868 --> 00:44:32,046
Isn't that wonderful?

856
00:44:32,070 --> 00:44:34,336
What does that have
to do with this case?

857
00:44:34,406 --> 00:44:37,206
It has everything to
do with it, Your Honor.

858
00:44:40,512 --> 00:44:43,713
Don't you see
that Mr. Richardson

859
00:44:43,782 --> 00:44:46,115
was able to kill

860
00:44:46,183 --> 00:44:50,520
Sally Hitchcock by
delayed reaction.

861
00:44:53,357 --> 00:44:56,325
And it shows me

862
00:44:56,394 --> 00:44:59,328
that you were
able to put yourself

863
00:44:59,397 --> 00:45:03,633
in the clear when
the poison took effect.

864
00:45:03,701 --> 00:45:05,434
This is ridiculous.

865
00:45:05,503 --> 00:45:07,381
I don't know what
you're talking about.

866
00:45:07,405 --> 00:45:08,704
The bandage!

867
00:45:08,773 --> 00:45:09,905
The bandage!

868
00:45:09,974 --> 00:45:12,107
You put poison in the bandage,

869
00:45:12,176 --> 00:45:13,642
and it's right here.

870
00:45:16,614 --> 00:45:19,482
I got it at the
coroner's office.

871
00:45:19,550 --> 00:45:22,518
See? See?

872
00:45:22,587 --> 00:45:24,153
There.

873
00:45:24,222 --> 00:45:26,366
Nobody paid any attention to it

874
00:45:26,390 --> 00:45:28,601
because they didn't
think it was important.

875
00:45:28,625 --> 00:45:30,270
Thank God they
didn't throw it away

876
00:45:30,294 --> 00:45:33,762
or we would never
have known, would we?

877
00:45:35,967 --> 00:45:38,267
You put...

878
00:45:38,336 --> 00:45:43,638
dimethyl sulfate
on that bandage...

879
00:45:43,707 --> 00:45:46,242
and you put it on
the back of her neck.

880
00:45:49,413 --> 00:45:51,491
Then you took her by the arm,

881
00:45:51,515 --> 00:45:54,895
smiled at her, took
her back to the party.

882
00:45:54,919 --> 00:45:59,221
And when she
walked away from you,

883
00:45:59,290 --> 00:46:03,259
you knew the poison

884
00:46:03,327 --> 00:46:05,995
was seeping slowly
through her body.

885
00:46:06,063 --> 00:46:09,464
And it's getting stronger

886
00:46:09,533 --> 00:46:11,845
and stronger and stronger,

887
00:46:11,869 --> 00:46:17,173
and when you were in a
whole nother part of the house,

888
00:46:17,241 --> 00:46:23,879
it seized her, collapsed
her breathing...

889
00:46:23,948 --> 00:46:27,082
and she collapsed and died.

890
00:46:30,888 --> 00:46:34,857
You killed her...
and this proves it.

891
00:46:38,462 --> 00:46:40,362
Nothing further.

892
00:46:42,133 --> 00:46:45,367
We find the defendant
David Tanney not guilty.

893
00:46:45,436 --> 00:46:47,348
Thank you, ladies and gentlemen.

894
00:46:47,372 --> 00:46:48,372
This court is adjourned.

895
00:46:49,240 --> 00:46:50,280
Thanks, Mr. Matlock.

896
00:46:51,475 --> 00:46:54,076
Thank you, Ms.
Thomas; thank you.

897
00:46:54,145 --> 00:46:55,845
Well, great job, Ben.

898
00:46:55,913 --> 00:46:58,114
Michelle... Hmm?

899
00:46:58,182 --> 00:46:59,414
Do me a favor.

900
00:47:02,420 --> 00:47:08,924
Take this hospital
gown and give it to Gert.

901
00:47:08,993 --> 00:47:11,126
She'll know what it means.

9999
00:00:0,500 --> 00:00:2,00
